{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-149955" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x-1)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f5464d6f1e9c48764bd8b4023d4ce84db663e21d17aea10bef9dfb63697aa2b"} {"question" "q-149955" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x-1):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/assets/9e2e705cf17a5dca362c23a23e4d10067ff4390a3f9464dddb6745d78986c02a.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x-1)$ is $x\\in [0,1].$ This means that $\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x-1)$ is undefined outside this interval.\n\nTherefore, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x-1)$ is undefined." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f5464d6f1e9c48764bd8b4023d4ce84db663e21d17aea10bef9dfb63697aa2b"} {"question" "q-149955" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bcc4e20e767142f92c28665f114a86c116c2091c1762d72c381143b455dbb22f"} {"question" "q-149955" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f5464d6f1e9c48764bd8b4023d4ce84db663e21d17aea10bef9dfb63697aa2b"} {"question" "q-149955" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\infty "] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\infty "] ["text" "Undefined"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f5464d6f1e9c48764bd8b4023d4ce84db663e21d17aea10bef9dfb63697aa2b"} {"question" "q-149955" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "Undefined"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f5464d6f1e9c48764bd8b4023d4ce84db663e21d17aea10bef9dfb63697aa2b"} {"question" "q-302689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x-2))=$\n\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f5464d6f1e9c48764bd8b4023d4ce84db663e21d17aea10bef9dfb63697aa2b"} {"question" "q-302689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x-2):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/assets/a7e36a5c534a63199ea97985f1301db0c7675adc8fa0d17f33735c61eec9e871.png)\n\nThe domain of   $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x-2)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nAs $x$ increases to $\\infty ,$ the graph tends to $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x-2)) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f5464d6f1e9c48764bd8b4023d4ce84db663e21d17aea10bef9dfb63697aa2b"} {"question" "q-302689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bcc4e20e767142f92c28665f114a86c116c2091c1762d72c381143b455dbb22f"} {"question" "q-302689" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f5464d6f1e9c48764bd8b4023d4ce84db663e21d17aea10bef9dfb63697aa2b"} {"question" "q-302689" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f5464d6f1e9c48764bd8b4023d4ce84db663e21d17aea10bef9dfb63697aa2b"} {"question" "q-339380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }2(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x+5))=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f5464d6f1e9c48764bd8b4023d4ce84db663e21d17aea10bef9dfb63697aa2b"} {"question" "q-339380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x+5):$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/assets/25cea33f2fc3a3bcdbc10ca03f93bd6059eb7d0a7dfcda5eb59f6f671387aea3.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x+5)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Moreover, from the graph, we see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x+5)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }2(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x+5))=2\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\pi .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f5464d6f1e9c48764bd8b4023d4ce84db663e21d17aea10bef9dfb63697aa2b"} {"question" "q-339380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bcc4e20e767142f92c28665f114a86c116c2091c1762d72c381143b455dbb22f"} {"question" "q-339380" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f5464d6f1e9c48764bd8b4023d4ce84db663e21d17aea10bef9dfb63697aa2b"} {"question" "q-339380" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f5464d6f1e9c48764bd8b4023d4ce84db663e21d17aea10bef9dfb63697aa2b"} {"question" "q-339477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\frac{1}{2}}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x))=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f5464d6f1e9c48764bd8b4023d4ce84db663e21d17aea10bef9dfb63697aa2b"} {"question" "q-339477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/assets/24f07da42a537ded7916fc2440dcf3ee1ccdfc81c7b027b47e97814fec059f5a.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)$ is $x\\in [-1,1].$\n\nNow, substituting $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\frac{1}{2}}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f5464d6f1e9c48764bd8b4023d4ce84db663e21d17aea10bef9dfb63697aa2b"} {"question" "q-339477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bcc4e20e767142f92c28665f114a86c116c2091c1762d72c381143b455dbb22f"} {"question" "q-339477" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f5464d6f1e9c48764bd8b4023d4ce84db663e21d17aea10bef9dfb63697aa2b"} {"question" "q-339477" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f5464d6f1e9c48764bd8b4023d4ce84db663e21d17aea10bef9dfb63697aa2b"} {"question" "q-339490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\sqrt{3}}sin\\,(\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x))=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f5464d6f1e9c48764bd8b4023d4ce84db663e21d17aea10bef9dfb63697aa2b"} {"question" "q-339490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/assets/68f1ebd0457e0c127f8ed6c979feba58196aa6bb43d97d211efa9b39bc33f637.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $x=\\sqrt{3}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\sqrt{3}}sin\\,(\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)) & =sin\\,(\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})) \\\\  & =sin\\,(\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f5464d6f1e9c48764bd8b4023d4ce84db663e21d17aea10bef9dfb63697aa2b"} {"question" "q-339490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bcc4e20e767142f92c28665f114a86c116c2091c1762d72c381143b455dbb22f"} {"question" "q-339490" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f5464d6f1e9c48764bd8b4023d4ce84db663e21d17aea10bef9dfb63697aa2b"} {"question" "q-339490" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f5464d6f1e9c48764bd8b4023d4ce84db663e21d17aea10bef9dfb63697aa2b"}] "usage" {"q-149955" []} "basis" 1392 "retractions" [[17592186184457 :question/problem "What is the value of $lim_(x → - ∞)\\arcsin (2x - 1)$?"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186181191 17592186181192 17592186181193 17592186181194 17592186181195] "immutable_fields" [[17592186181190 :answer-field/correct] [17592186181190 :answer-fiel